WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:05.200
Alien: Covenant went through various changes
during its development ranging from its title

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.400
changing from "Paradise Lost" to "Covenant",
to director Ridley Scott changing his mind

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:13.160
about whether Elizabeth Shaw would return,
to major scenes shown in promotional material

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:14.160
that we never saw in the movie.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:18.280
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here,
and in this video I'm going to break down

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:23.070
everything we know so far about what was deleted
and rejected from the final cut of Alien:

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:24.070
Covenant.

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:27.720
My Alien: Covenant merchandise giveaway is
also running on this video so be sure to leave

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:31.990
a comment about the movie and subscribe for
a chance to win one of these two awesome packs

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:33.130
of merch.

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:37.030
And just before we get stuck in, obviously,
there are spoilers ahead, so be aware of that

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:38.940
if you haven't yet seen the movie.

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:43.600
First, let's take a look a major scene nearly
four and a half minutes long that was completely

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:45.570
cut from the final movie.

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:49.579
Fox actually released a clip of the scene
online and called it "The Last Supper", a

00:00:49.579 --> 00:00:54.000
title which, like so much in the Alien prequels,
has strong religious connotations.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:58.390
The deleted scene is a really great introduction
to the crew of the Covenant and is set before

00:00:58.390 --> 00:01:02.179
they go into cryo-sleep, so that means it
was meant to appear before the opening scene

00:01:02.179 --> 00:01:04.250
on the ship in the final movie.

00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:06.630
"Follow the light."

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:10.600
"How do you feel Daniels?"

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:11.600
"Fine."

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:13.770
"Any dizziness, nausea?"

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:15.360
"I'm fine."

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:18.940
It's such a shame the scene was cut as there
are so many nice little moments that give

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:23.759
some real insight into individual characters
and the dynamics between the various members

00:01:23.759 --> 00:01:24.759
of the group.

00:01:24.759 --> 00:01:29.320
For example, you see the differences in personality
and views between Billy Crudup's second-in-command,

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:34.719
Oram, and James Franco's Captain Branson,
and also Danny McBride's pilot Tennessee.

00:01:34.719 --> 00:01:37.479
"It's a hell of a view, innit?"

00:01:37.479 --> 00:01:39.280
"It is, pure majesty."

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:41.990
"I dunno what you're talking about.

00:01:41.990 --> 00:01:43.359
Kinda spooks me out.

00:01:43.359 --> 00:01:45.829
Big old sea of nothing, huh."

00:01:45.829 --> 00:01:51.000
And you get a real sense of the simmering
tensions between Oram and the others.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:52.820
"Tennessee can be a jerk."

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:55.890
"Why are you speaking so loudly?

00:01:55.890 --> 00:01:56.890
He's right there."

00:01:56.890 --> 00:02:00.290
"I know, he's.., he can't hear me, he's drunk,
again he's always drunk."

00:02:00.290 --> 00:02:02.930
"His wife is even drunker, have you seen that?"

00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:06.560
On top of that, seeing the crew's couples
interact with each other would definitely

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:10.430
have helped me feel a closer connection to
their characters and therefore would have

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:14.260
made me care a bit more about their deaths
when each of them inevitably gets picked off

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:15.330
as the movie progresses.

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:19.510
"I just wanted to say hey before I jet out,
I'm feeling kinda queasy."

00:02:19.510 --> 00:02:21.080
"What, you not feeling good?"

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:22.160
"I'm just burning up."

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:26.250
"I thought we were gonna have one more drink
before we went into cryo-sleep.

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:28.030
Who's gonna lead us in our toast?"

00:02:28.030 --> 00:02:32.030
"Have Danny do something, she'll know what
to say."

00:02:32.030 --> 00:02:33.360
"Aye, aye captain."

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:34.640
"Make sure everyone behaves."

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:37.010
"Oh yeah, you can count on me."

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:39.319
"Good night."

00:02:39.319 --> 00:02:42.790
"Good night, captain."

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:45.100
"Feel better."

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:48.569
"Is he gone?"

00:02:48.569 --> 00:02:49.720
"Yep."

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:52.030
"Let's party."

00:02:52.030 --> 00:02:59.520
And, of course, this scene would have meant
that James Franco would have got a bit of

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:03.560
real screen time interacting with his crew
instead of us just seeing his character burnt

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:07.790
alive inside a sleeping pod or rock-climbing
in a video message for his wife.

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:12.620
And, yes, the scene even includes a bit of
foreshadowing of Captain Branson's fate when

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:15.989
he says to the rest of the crew that he's
heading off to cryo-sleep early because he's

00:03:15.989 --> 00:03:17.920
feeling queasy and "burning up".

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:22.500
There's also a fun easter egg to the original
Alien chest-bursting scene in what turns out

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:25.400
to be a little fake-out by director Ridley
Scott.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:30.150
The bit I'm talking about is when coms expert
Upworth, who's played by Callie Hernandez,

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:34.270
suddenly struggles to breathe as they're eating,
which is a call-back to the scene from Alien

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:38.750
where John Hurt's character Kane has a similar
reaction during their meal, but in Hurt's

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:42.160
case it's because a Chestburster is about
to explode out of him.

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:46.159
And there's another nice shout-out to that
choking scene in Alien when Danny McBride's

00:03:46.159 --> 00:03:51.069
character Tennessee echoes Parker's words
to Kane, 'the food's not that bad!'

00:03:51.069 --> 00:03:52.819
"You alright?"

00:03:52.819 --> 00:03:57.480
"Babe, the food's not that bad."

00:03:57.480 --> 00:03:59.910
"Babe, babe!"

00:03:59.910 --> 00:04:02.349
"You OK?"

00:04:02.349 --> 00:04:13.829
"Down the 

00:04:13.829 --> 00:04:14.829
wrong pipe."

00:04:14.829 --> 00:04:16.269
"Thank you."

00:04:16.269 --> 00:04:18.720
"I've got your back."

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:22.220
"Ooh, that was a joke, right?"

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:27.039
And the deleted scene finished with a heartfelt
and optimistic speech from Daniels to the

00:04:27.039 --> 00:04:31.150
crew, which again I think would have enhanced
how the audience related to the Covenant's

00:04:31.150 --> 00:04:32.150
characters.

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:34.460
"So what about that speech Daniels?"

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:36.410
"Oh, I haven't prepared..."

00:04:36.410 --> 00:04:42.380
"Sorry, Jake asked me to say something if
that's OK?"

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:43.590
"Please."

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:48.990
"You've all sacrificed so much to be here.

00:04:48.990 --> 00:04:53.270
To be a part of this.

00:04:53.270 --> 00:05:01.139
It's the first ever large-scale colonisation
mission to come this far into our galaxy.

00:05:01.139 --> 00:05:03.190
We're making history.

00:05:03.190 --> 00:05:13.410
Everyone back on Earth is really grateful
for your hard work and your courage.

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:21.600
I just wanna say I couldn't pick a better
bunch of jerks to marrooned on a distant planet

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:22.600
with."

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:26.280
"So, erm, to the Covenant!"

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:28.630
"To the Covenant!"

00:05:28.630 --> 00:05:33.660
James Franco's Branson and Katherine Waterston's
Daniels were also involved in another deleted

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:36.270
scene, though this one was set in their New
York apartment.

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:40.360
The cut scene would have set up the backstory
in more detail for why Branson and Daniels

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:43.790
wanted to build a house on the lake when they
reached the remote planet they were about

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:45.120
to journey to.

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:48.720
Although this would have helped build more
of Daniels' backstory, given James Franco

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:53.130
more time on screen, and afforded us greater
insight into their connection as a couple,

00:05:53.130 --> 00:05:56.539
it seems like this scene could have felt a
bit too slow right at the beginning of the

00:05:56.539 --> 00:06:00.491
movie, which is where it would have appeared,
so perhaps it was cut for time and to get

00:06:00.491 --> 00:06:05.960
the story moving along a bit more briskly
than it would have done if this had been included.

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:10.460
Another lengthy deleted scene, also released
online by Fox, features Noomi Rapace's Elizabeth

00:06:10.460 --> 00:06:12.819
Shaw and Michael Fassbender's David.

00:06:12.819 --> 00:06:17.500
In the scene, David provides a voiceover where
he explains what happened at the end of Prometheus

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:20.930
and how he escaped with Elizabeth on an Engineer's
ship.

00:06:20.930 --> 00:06:25.630
A little piece of the dialogue from this voiceover
is in the final movie although it's used in

00:06:25.630 --> 00:06:26.630
a different scene.

00:06:26.630 --> 00:06:30.550
There are also some nice moments in this deleted
segment where we get to see the interaction

00:06:30.550 --> 00:06:34.240
between Elizabeth and David, including how
she took care of him and put him back together,

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:37.830
and there's a hint at what feels like a bond
building between them.

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:44.910
"After we made contact with the Engineers,
the Prometheus was destroyed.

00:06:44.910 --> 00:06:49.810
All hands were lost, but I escaped with Elizabeth
in one of their ships.

00:06:49.810 --> 00:06:53.919
I was badly injured on our mission.

00:06:53.919 --> 00:06:56.210
She put me back together.

00:06:56.210 --> 00:07:03.460
I never experienced such compassion, certainly
not from Mr Weyland, or from any human."

00:07:03.460 --> 00:07:05.900
"Green to green.

00:07:05.900 --> 00:07:08.340
Red to red.

00:07:08.340 --> 00:07:12.410
It's meant to be simple."

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:15.669
"I'm doing my best."

00:07:15.669 --> 00:07:21.360
"You're very kind at heart you know."

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:26.930
"We were able to activate their ship and set
course for their homeworld.

00:07:26.930 --> 00:07:31.830
We were finally going to meet our creator."

00:07:31.830 --> 00:07:33.060
"How long?"

00:07:33.060 --> 00:07:34.889
"Impossible to say."

00:07:34.889 --> 00:07:39.180
"What if they're no better than us?"

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:43.470
"So long as they are no worse."

00:07:43.470 --> 00:07:44.699
"Sleep tight.

00:07:44.699 --> 00:07:47.210
I'll awake you when we arrive."

00:07:47.210 --> 00:07:58.110
I also liked how this final "sleep tight"
that David says to Elizabeth, just before

00:07:58.110 --> 00:08:02.289
putting her back into cryo-sleep, is later
mirrored at the end of Alien: Covenant with

00:08:02.289 --> 00:08:06.520
the much more menacing, "sleep tight don't
let the bed bugs bite", that David says to

00:08:06.520 --> 00:08:11.879
Daniels as he sends her into cryo-sleep after
it finally dawns on her that he's not Walter.

00:08:11.879 --> 00:08:17.099
I think if the final film had included these
moments, the implied kindness in them between

00:08:17.099 --> 00:08:21.030
Shaw and David would have made what he did
to her later when he used her body for his

00:08:21.030 --> 00:08:24.960
genetic experiments even more horrifying and
impactful.

00:08:24.960 --> 00:08:29.020
At the end of the deleted scene, we also get
a hint at why David made the shocking decision

00:08:29.020 --> 00:08:32.479
to wipe out the Engineers when he reached
the planet.

00:08:32.479 --> 00:08:36.770
After putting Shaw to sleep, David wanders
in the dark among the Engineers' exoskeletons

00:08:36.770 --> 00:08:41.210
and he explains how he spent the time on the
journey learning about the Engineers, which

00:08:41.210 --> 00:08:44.940
suggests he discovered something about them
that made him as disappointed with them as

00:08:44.940 --> 00:08:49.320
he was with human beings, and this led him
to destroy the Engineers when he arrived on

00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:51.110
their planet.

00:08:51.110 --> 00:08:53.880
And there were a few other deleted scenes
on board the Covenant.

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:57.950
The first shows some footage of Daniels talking
to "Mother" and in another she's playing cards

00:08:57.950 --> 00:09:02.090
with Tennessee and it looks like his wife
Faris might be with him, so this could be

00:09:02.090 --> 00:09:04.820
a scene before the crew land on the planet.

00:09:04.820 --> 00:09:09.980
"Mother, how long have we been travelling?"

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:11.900
"Approximately 24 days."

00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:14.820
"Is there anything for breakfast other than
oatmeal."

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:18.470
"Rations have been selected for optimal nutritional
content."

00:09:18.470 --> 00:09:25.590
"Mother, is there a planet in the known universe
where a full house beats a straight flush."

00:09:25.590 --> 00:09:27.360
"Don't bring Mother into this.

00:09:27.360 --> 00:09:30.180
Mother, stay out of this."

00:09:30.180 --> 00:09:32.510
"Mother?"

00:09:32.510 --> 00:09:36.720
And there's a cut scene with Daniels hunting
the Protomorph that emerged inside the Covenant

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:39.080
where "Mother" suddenly informs her it's "four
metres above you".

00:09:39.080 --> 00:09:40.080
"Where is this goddamm thing?"

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:41.540
"Four meters above you."

00:09:41.540 --> 00:09:51.390
In fact, that bit of the deleted scene reminded
me of the moment in Alien where Lambert is

00:09:51.390 --> 00:09:55.640
talking to Dallas while he's in the air ducts
and he suddenly discovers the Xenomorph is

00:09:55.640 --> 00:09:56.640
upon him.

00:09:56.640 --> 00:10:01.230
So, did you enjoy Alien: Covenant and were
you happy with the final cut of the movie?

00:10:01.230 --> 00:10:05.460
Were there any scenes you wish had been kept
in the film or anything you would like to

00:10:05.460 --> 00:10:06.690
have seen cut out?

